"""
Run FastSurfer with one command on every system: in its container image, or on a Mac with Apple silicon
with the macOS package.

Takes the flags of run_fastsurfer.sh and runs them in the official image with Apptainer, Singularity
or Docker, whichever is installed:

    ./fastsurfer --t1 data/t1.nii.gz --sd results --sid subject1

--exec runs another program of the image with the arguments after it: brun_fastsurfer.sh and
long_fastsurfer.sh as FastSurfer itself, and any other program, e.g. --exec nib-convert in.mgz
out.nii.gz, in the current directory.

It runs the FastSurfer release image installed on the machine (the newest release if there is none,
or the image --image names), picks the image type that fits the NVIDIA GPU and driver (or, without
one, the experimental ROCm image for an AMD GPU, or the CPU image), downloads it once,
shares every file and directory the flags name with the container at the same path, passes the
FreeSurfer license from $FS_LICENSE if --fs_license is not given, and runs the container as the
calling user. On a Mac with Apple silicon, it runs the installed macOS package instead, with the
same choice among installed versions.

Only the Python standard library is used, so this runs with the system Python of a cluster,
without FastSurfer installed. It has no .py suffix, so a copy next to other Python code cannot
shadow the package fastsurfer.
"""

